{*
	Constructs that exist only in the Latte 2 line, kept apart from the general
	templates for the same reason latte-3-only.latte is: a file that is red
	whichever version the project uses teaches nobody anything.

	Nothing here may be underlined. The playground's composer.json declares
	latte/latte ^2.11.7, so this file is the one that matches the project as it
	stands; every line in it is either gone or a compile error in Latte 3.

	  - {includeblock} was removed outright; {import} plus {include} is the 3.x
	    way of writing it.
	  - |noiterator survived into 3.0.6 and the argument grammar rejects it from
	    3.0.7 on.
	  - {syntax latte} is the 2.11 spelling; 3.0.2 dropped it, and 3.0.24 brought
	    the same behaviour back under the name {syntax single}.
	  - {else} and {elseif} are ordinary tags in 2.11 and inner tags of {if} in
	    3.x, so writing one without its parent compiles only here.
*}
{var $items = [1, 2, 3]}
{var $show = true}

{includeblock 'inheritance-blocks.latte'}

{foreach $items|noiterator as $item}
	<span>{$item}</span>
{/foreach}

{* Latte 2 matches these names case-insensitively, so the camelCase spelling of
   the same directive is the same directive. *}
{foreach $items|noIterator as $item}
	<span>{$item}</span>
{/foreach}

{syntax latte}
<p>{$show ? 'braces work as usual' : ''}</p>

{* {snippet} and {snippetArea} are core tags in 2.11; from Latte 3 they come
   from nette/application instead, so a project without it loses them. *}
{snippet counter}
	<p>{$items|length}</p>
{/snippet}
